//
//  Signing.xcconfig
//  Sycamore
//
//  The three build settings that are a property of *whoever is building*, rather than of the
//  project: the team the profile is requested from, the App ID it is requested for, and the
//  entitlements that App ID is allowed to claim. They live here instead of in `project.pbxproj`
//  so a second person can build on their own phone without editing — and then committing — a
//  file that would break everyone else's device build.
//
//  The values below are the real ones: team `FYQ358R59X`, the App ID that has Sign In with Apple
//  ticked, and the entitlement that claims it. That is what CI and the maintainer build with,
//  and it is what you get if you do nothing.
//
//  To build under a different Apple ID, write `Config/Signing.local.xcconfig` — it is
//  gitignored, it is `#include?`d below (the `?` means "if it exists"), and it overrides any of
//  the three by setting the `SYCAMORE_*` variable rather than the build setting itself. Copy
//  `Signing.local.xcconfig.example` and fill it in.
//
//  Set these in the file, not in Xcode's Signing & Capabilities tab. Anything you change there
//  is written straight into `project.pbxproj`, where it wins over this file and lands in your
//  next commit.
//

// The team automatic signing asks for a provisioning profile. A free Apple ID has one too — its
// ten-character Personal Team ID, from Xcode → Settings → Accounts.
SYCAMORE_DEVELOPMENT_TEAM = FYQ358R59X

// App IDs are a single global namespace, so this string is claimed and cannot be claimed twice.
// A second developer needs their own — `com.yourname.sycamore` — which also means their build is
// a different app to Apple, to Supabase's Apple provider, and to the phone, which will install
// it alongside rather than over the top.
SYCAMORE_BUNDLE_ID = com.cjgimena.app

// Set empty to build with no entitlements at all. Free Apple IDs must: a Personal Team cannot
// sign `com.apple.developer.applesignin`, and Xcode rejects the build outright rather than
// dropping the claim. What that costs is only the "Continue with Apple" route — the email and
// six-digit code path is untouched, and a DEBUG build's Apple button bypasses to the offline
// store anyway (see `SignInView.signInWithApple`).
SYCAMORE_ENTITLEMENTS = Config/Sycamore.entitlements

#include? "Signing.local.xcconfig"

// Assigned after the include so the local file only has to state the `SYCAMORE_*` value it
// wants, in any order, and never these three names.
DEVELOPMENT_TEAM = $(SYCAMORE_DEVELOPMENT_TEAM)
PRODUCT_BUNDLE_IDENTIFIER = $(SYCAMORE_BUNDLE_ID)
CODE_SIGN_ENTITLEMENTS = $(SYCAMORE_ENTITLEMENTS)
